pufferlib-metal: an unofficial Apple Metal 4 backend for PufferLib 5.

Upstream base: PufferAI/PufferLib branch 5.0, revision
ea7f989371270d2948f96728bda8aec5e7634a4c.

Third-party code and assets inherited unchanged from upstream PufferLib retain
their own licenses (see vendor/ and resources/*).
See [THIRD_PARTY.md](THIRD_PARTY.md) for the inventory of declared sources,
licenses and notices, including missing provenance. It is not a legal determination.

PufferLib is Copyright (c) 2022 PufferAI, MIT License (see LICENSE).

Portions of the Metal backend are adapted from Valtteri Valo's Metal 4 backend
for PufferLib 4.0 (https://github.com/valtterivalo/PufferLib, branch
metal-local; see also PufferAI/PufferLib PR #532), also MIT licensed:
  - src/metal/runtime.mm: device, buffer wrapping and residency handling, adapted
    from src/metal/platform.{h,mm}
  - src/metal/shaders/gemm.metal: split-K GEMM tile loop structure, adapted from
    sgemm_ksplit and platform.mm
Thanks to Valtteri for the prior art that made this port much easier.

Portions of src/metal/shaders/muon.metal and src/metal/shaders/wide_muon.h adapt the explicit SIMD shuffle
reduction mechanism in MLX mlx/backend/metal/kernels/reduction/ops.h and
8x8 fragment coordinates in mlx/backend/metal/kernels/steel/gemm/mma.h, pinned
commit 56c2bf9236d929097f61e2c6e55be4e4bb6da249
(https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx). Modifications: retain Puffer's lane-local
accumulation and wide-norm shared-memory tree through stride 32; finish only the last
five matching additions with shuffles, with a threadgroup handoff where needed;
use spatial FP32 MMA fragments for the H64 Muon gram-buffer/update stages,
retaining Puffer's struct ABI, explicit storage conversion and alpha/beta finish.

